  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the blackeye peas and soak them in water for at least 4 hours or overnight.",
    "In a pot, combine water, kombu, shiitake, and bring to a gentle boil; simmer for 15 minutes, then remove the kombu.",
    "Add the soaked peas, diced onion, minced garlic, and minced ginger to the pot; simmer for 45 minutes until the peas are tender.",
    "Stir in tamari soy sauce, mirin, and sesame oil; season with salt if desired, and simmer for an additional 5 minutes.",
    "Remove the pot from heat and let the soup rest for 2 minutes to allow flavors to meld.",
    "Serve the soup hot, garnishing with sliced scallions."
